{"c":[{"id":"0059496448e90edc","sum":"Script-only writer; clone-portable notes; onboarding=init; 3.11; .summ; unique-prefix; heal raw JSON; root how_to; catalog git-visible /.summem/; note prints Saved.; surgery.py deletes","tree":{"c":[{"id":"457442361bf86149","sum":"Script is the only writer; tox py311-py314; nested recall; skipped-a-pack; notes are clone-portable (no OptMem in the prompt); onboarding is init; version/Release Please/coverage are product; note prints Saved.; surgery.py deletes; AGPL plus 0BSD+§7 in the summem header only.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"3d8e48dcd08287d1","sum":"AGENT_BIN vs CLI_NAME; VISION/ROADMAP retired (README+atlas+notes+MB). tox py311-py314; nested recall; skipped-a-pack. Script is the only writer (files are the work). Note membership is clone-portability; no OptMem in the prompt. Onboarding: docs/agents-prompt.md lockstep.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"4078d7c411ce74e3","sum":"AGENT_BIN vs CLI_NAME; VISION/ROADMAP retired for README+atlas+notes+memory-bank. tox py311-py314 no result cache; nested recall; skipped-a-pack on bad sibling; script is the only writer.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"5e4f97413b312154","sum":"Run: uses AGENT_BIN; help catalog uses CLI_NAME. VISION/ROADMAP retired; living docs are README, docs/architecture/ (atlas), docs/notes.md leftovers, and the memory-bank.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"667b5bd40e9be23d","sum":"Run: line uses AGENT_BIN (.summem/summem); help catalog uses CLI_NAME. VISION/ROADMAP sunset; living docs are README, docs/, and the memory-bank.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260820T023238Z-bbf825b6f524dcb6","text":"Nap Run: line uses AGENT_BIN (.summem/summem), same as the baked prompt; usage_text keeps CLI_NAME (summem).","type":"note"},{"name":"20260820T025054Z-8222dbc737ce85a4","text":"VISION.md and ROADMAP.md are being sunset: leftovers go under docs/; README and memory-bank become the living docs; VISION is no longer the design contract.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"5e022ef533bec842","sum":"VISION.md and ROADMAP.md retired. Living docs are README, docs/architecture/ (the atlas), docs/notes.md leftovers, and the memory-bank. VISION is not the contract.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260820T025220Z-1a52749b783612ee","text":"docs-sunset plan: VISION/ROADMAP retire; architecture lives at docs/architecture/; leftovers (sqlite, hooks, cover(T), pack-size, hot margin) at docs/notes.md; README is the public face.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260820T030457Z-f1b0d73acb7f8b59","text":"VISION.md and ROADMAP.md are gone. Living docs are README, docs/architecture/, docs/notes.md, and the memory-bank. The architecture page is the atlas; VISION is not the contract.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"746cce2a386de2cd","sum":"tox is py311-py314 pytest, no result cache unless proven on this suite; recall matches nested nap captions; zoom/recall warn 'skipped a pack' on an unreadable sibling children file (wake silent). Script-written files are part of the work; the script is the only writer.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"29530a97880a269e","sum":"tox is the pytest suite on CPython 3.11–3.14 (no 3.10; no test-result cache unless proven on this tmp_path/worktree suite); recall matches nested nap captions; zoom/recall print 'skipped a pack' on stderr for an unreadable sibling children file; wake stays silent","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260820T034719Z-9ead1d6adb1f23f2","text":"Niko L2 tox-pytest-runner: one tox command for pytest on CPython 3.11–3.14 (no 3.10); skip test-result cache unless proven on this tmp_path/worktree suite","type":"note"},{"name":"20260820T035449Z-38690d9f52484de6","text":"recall matches nested NapChild.sum captions; zoom/recall print 'skipped a pack' on stderr when they skip an unreadable sibling children file; wake stays silent","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1cd145ba45ef49e6","sum":"tox is the suite (py311-py314, no result cache). Files the script writes are part of the work: git-add them; the script is the only writer.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260820T040400Z-6f72c4e24f7307a3","text":"tox is the suite command: tox.ini package=skip, py311-py314, no test-result cache; 211 pytest. This uv only had 3.14.0rc3.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260820T044725Z-82b67eae5e042401","text":"After note or nap, git add the files the script wrote and commit them; the script stays the only writer.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"97fbdbf480d21d0c","sum":"Script-written files are part of the work (not untracked). Note membership is clone-portability; do not name OptMem in the prompt. Too long: N/limit L; unknown id on identity-miss says copy from wake. Onboarding is docs/agents-prompt.md lockstep; TDD skips consumer Actions YAML.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"0b347fe3d88d5969","sum":"Files the script writes are part of the work; do not leave them untracked. Note membership is clone-portability on its own sentence; do not name OptMem in the prompt. Over-long note/nap prints Too long: N bytes, limit L; unknown id on identity-miss says copy from wake.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"4826b3cd066a8db2","sum":"Files the script writes are part of the work; do not leave them untracked. prompt-commit-notes archived (PR #15).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260820T143121Z-499b95db35c236dc","text":"Prompt: files the script writes are part of the work; do not leave them untracked. Not a separate git add procedure.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260820T143747Z-07042dccd58a8627","text":"prompt-commit-notes archived: files the script writes are part of your work; do not leave them untracked. Draft PR #15.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0e2730939d36cf17","sum":"Note membership is clone-portability on its own sentence; do not name OptMem in the prompt. Over-long note/nap prints Too long: N bytes, limit L; unknown id on identity-miss says copy from wake.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260820T144333Z-54317d52fae15bc6","text":"Note membership: session spawn 'document this machine gap' beat the baked filter because it is a trailing clause in the mandatory-note paragraph. Store/CLI stay; split the test onto its own clone-portability sentence. Do not name OptMem in the prompt.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260820T150951Z-48c09749f6b4d942","text":"Over-long note and nap captions print Too long: N bytes, limit L. Accented characters cost 2 bytes. Compress it further. Identity-miss unknown id says copy from wake; a missing children file does not.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"528f08ae8bb4cf55","sum":"Register Memories notes clone-portable facts (dump vs membership split); dump line does not say git forever. Onboarding is docs/agents-prompt.md lockstep with prompt_text(); TDD does not govern consumer Actions YAML that only invokes a third-party action.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"e2a8c1aafb975d12","sum":"Baked Register Memories: note a fact another contributor would still need; membership is clone-portability on its own sentence (dump vs membership split). Dump line no longer says git forever.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260820T152829Z-ff3349020923cee6","text":"Baked Register Memories: note when another contributor would still need the fact; membership is clone-portability on its own sentence. Dump line no longer says git forever.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260820T165146Z-3869ac160fa1eda4","text":"Draft PR #18: baked Register Memories splits dump from clone-portability membership; no store/CLI change.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"89acc35894e248e2","sum":"Onboarding is docs/agents-prompt.md, lockstep with prompt_text(); do not select wrapping init output. TDD does not govern consumer Actions YAML that only invokes a third-party action; it would if SumMem were an Action.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260820T184134Z-2efc5cdcb2d8b149","text":"Onboarding prompt is docs/agents-prompt.md, lockstep with prompt_text(); do not select wrapping init output.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260820T193911Z-1a2508c0f3d6386f","text":"TDD does not govern GitHub Actions YAML that only invokes a third-party action; it would if SumMem were an Action.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"7adc29ef51880740","sum":"Onboarding is init; version/Release Please/coverage are product; note prints Saved.; surgery.py emergency delete; AGPL plus 0BSD+§7 in the summem header only.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"460feb3ed8c0607d","sum":"Onboarding is summem init (prompt_text); version prints __version__, Release Please tracks extra-files, consumer Actions YAML is not product TDD. Coverage: pytest-cov measures the no-suffix driver; tox -e coverage uploads lcov.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"1b57bafcd1f51c08","sum":"Onboarding is summem init (prompt_text()); version-tracking archived (PR #22): version prints __version__, Release Please extra-files; consumer Actions YAML is not product TDD.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"9280565a8f63c495","sum":"Onboarding is summem init (prompt_text()), not a docs/agents-prompt.md copy. summem version prints __version__; Release Please extra-files bump repo-root summem.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260820T194852Z-ea2b60e530376ca4","text":"ship-prompt-file archived; onboarding is docs/agents-prompt.md; draft PR #21.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260820T195810Z-0def08186d21b807","text":"summem version prints __version__; Release Please simple extra-files bump repo-root summem via x-release-please-version.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"eacada5aac0af230","sum":"version-tracking archived (PR #22): summem version prints __version__; Release Please extra-files; consumer Actions YAML is not product TDD (same class as .cursor-rules#116).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260820T195859Z-a205a695beb1a648","text":"Preflight FAIL on consumer release-please.yaml was the same class as Texarkanine/.cursor-rules#116 (TDD encoding of tooling as product).","type":"note"},{"name":"20260820T203536Z-5ee598da385c9137","text":"version-tracking archived: summem version prints __version__; Release Please simple extra-files on repo-root summem; PR #22.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"94271e53e4e390e8","sum":"Coverage: pytest-cov measures the no-suffix driver; tox -e coverage uploads lcov (PR #23).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"9c098318cdba7a6c","sum":"pytest-cov --cov=summem measures the no-suffix driver; tox -e coverage writes coverage/lcov.info (lcov SF path summem), while default tox stays coverage-free.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260820T204638Z-78eb1773319c702b","text":"pytest-cov --cov=summem measures the no-suffix shebang; lcov SF path is summem.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260820T205716Z-2ff58bd8d1240b01","text":"tox -e coverage writes coverage/lcov.info via pytest-cov --cov=summem; default tox stays coverage-free.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e4a889eeb8ef62b8","sum":"Draft PR #23 archived: tox -e coverage uploads lcov to Codecov; README badge.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260820T210212Z-1d110b7fc5fdd2af","text":"Draft PR #23: tox -e coverage uploads lcov to Codecov; README badge.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260820T213032Z-d2f8289f08d361a6","text":"codecov-upload archived: tox -e coverage uploads lcov; README badge; draft PR #23.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"687bf44f7f1d1ca9","sum":"Root wake labels a non-empty git-root document; note prints Saved. then maybe a fold request; emergency delete is surgery.py; note-ack-surgery L4 capped; AGPL program, 0BSD+§7 in the summem header only (PR #32)","tree":{"c":[{"id":"75ea440c81cc93d7","sum":"Root wake labels a non-empty git-root document; note prints Saved. then maybe a fold request (do not retry); emergency delete is surgery.py, not a subcommand","tree":{"c":[{"id":"08c734f3ed243af8","sum":"Root wake labels a non-empty git-root document; emergency delete is surgery.py (zipper out, unlink one note, heal_view), not a subcommand","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260820T233118Z-a3b7a5135628a4f0","text":"Root wake prints == Project-root Memories == when the git-root document is non-empty, catalog or not. Pull wakes stay unlabeled.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260821T155541Z-842d10e98fbc74de","text":"Emergency delete is repo-root surgery.py, not a summem subcommand: zipper break-out of containing naps, unlink that one note, heal_view; it does not rewrite git history or write nap captions.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"8c9885aa12cc2275","sum":"Successful note prints Saved. then maybe a fold request; the nap is extra work on already-stored memory - do not retry the same note (PR #29 closed #27)","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260821T160046Z-f394b9340bcc2577","text":"Successful summem note prints Saved. then maybe a fold request. A nap after note is extra work on already-stored memory; do not retry the same note.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260821T160735Z-ea1c2c79f1a46533","text":"Draft PR #29 feat/note-ack closes #27: successful note prints Saved. then maybe a fold request; do not retry the same note.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"4d2319ab67d787e7","sum":"note-ack-surgery L4 capped (#29+#30); program is AGPL, 0BSD prompt and §7 invocation live only in the summem header; LICENSE verbatim; surgery.py stock AGPL (PR #32)","tree":{"c":[{"id":"98bd8ec9648a6a8b","sum":"note-ack-surgery L4 capped (#29+#30 merged, archive on main). Program is AGPL; 0BSD prompt and §7 invocation permission live in the summem header (authoritative); LICENSE stays verbatim AGPL; surgery.py echoes invocation only.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260821T172411Z-b5e0645705ca3183","text":"L4 note-ack-surgery capped: #29 and #30 merged; capstone archive memory-bank/archive/enhancements/20260821-note-ack-surgery.md on main.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260823T191515Z-afdba13a71a9e2b8","text":"Program is AGPL; prompt template is 0BSD and invocation is a section 7 additional permission, both in the summem header (authoritative). LICENSE stays verbatim AGPL; surgery.py echoes invocation only.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"55a93401f0823aa5","sum":"surgery.py stays stock AGPL; §7 invocation + 0BSD prompt live only in the summem header; agpl-carve-outs archived as PR #32","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260823T191944Z-6b284f7ab99096b8","text":"surgery.py stays stock AGPL. The section 7 invocation permission and 0BSD prompt terms live only in the summem header.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260823T193232Z-015b467b7a2c8879","text":"agpl-carve-outs archived to memory-bank/archive/enhancements/20260823-agpl-carve-outs.md; draft PR #32.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"30168750c4c633f7","sum":"format_wake_line shared; named_ids catches tree-parse; fold_request --path if walk-up misses. Root how_to under Usage. Onboarding=init; 3.11 floor. Captions .summ. SLOBAC proofs; #48 14/60-63. Zoom pin=selected nap. Catalog git-visible /.summem/; unique-prefix; heal raw JSON.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"f8270fbd698a350a","sum":"Wake/recall/zoom share format_wake_line; named_ids catches tree-parse errors; fold_request adds --path when walk-up would miss. Root wake prints how_to under Usage; skip a second when that block is still readable. Onboarding is init; 3.11 floor is right after import sys.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"3f064eaca2fcf0fe","sum":"Wake/recall/zoom share format_wake_line (dated leaves, prefixed packs); recall matches text and captions; walkers enqueue NapChild ids from the tree; fold_request adds --path REL when walk-up would miss; 3.11 floor is right after import sys; named_ids catches _TREE_PARSE_ERRORS.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"f47ceea4c51ec638","sum":"Wake/recall/zoom share xN TOKEN: body; leaves are x1 YYYY-MM-DD: no parens; packs have no day; recall matches note text and captions; fold_request Run: adds --path REL when walk-up from $PWD would miss the store.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"15146632137cf430","sum":"fold_request Run: adds --path REL when walk-up from $PWD would miss the store; wake dates leaves x1 YYYY-MM-DD: from the stamp, packs stay xN prefix: caption.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260823T212302Z-619f7114a3c3445b","text":"fold_request Run: includes --path REL when walk-up from $PWD would not select the folded store.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260824T142559Z-853c6c0b6ec510e9","text":"Wake leaf lines are x1 (YYYY-MM-DD): text from the filename stamp; nap lines stay xN prefix: caption with no day.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"87f86d77a75e4841","sum":"Wake/recall/zoom share xN TOKEN: body; leaves are x1 YYYY-MM-DD: with no parens; recall matches note text and nap captions, not grain, day, or id prefix.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260824T143849Z-bb7956f2f4651e25","text":"Wake leaf line is x1 YYYY-MM-DD: text, no parens; same xN TOKEN: body grammar as a pack.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260824T163806Z-5d0f4e137b683d7f","text":"Zoom and recall print the same wake grammar as wake (dated leaves, unique-prefix packs); recall matches note text and nap captions, not grain, day, or id prefix.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"9f77cab1df115c25","sum":"Wake/recall/zoom share format_wake_line and enqueue NapChild ids from the tree; 3.11 floor is immediately after import sys; named_ids catches _TREE_PARSE_ERRORS including AttributeError; agent-display-unify is PR #37.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"38ea7198a3688568","sum":"Wake/recall/zoom share format_wake_line; proof walkers enqueue NapChild ids from the children tree, not zoom stdout; agent-display-unify archived as PR #37.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260824T165407Z-a27fb3a92805a5d6","text":"Recall and zoom print format_wake_line like wake; proof walkers enqueue NapChild ids from the children tree, not zoom stdout tokens.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260824T173019Z-27bced2c4e108fab","text":"agent-display-unify archived: wake/recall/zoom share format_wake_line; PR #37 on labelling.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1fcbcf0346304c1f","sum":"3.11 floor is immediately after import sys so 3.10 prints SumMem needs Python 3.11 or newer; named_ids catches _TREE_PARSE_ERRORS including AttributeError on a non-mapping child.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260824T174425Z-833402129b2e4377","text":"require_python in main() is too late: module-level import tomllib dies on Python 3.10 before SumMem needs Python 3.11 or newer.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260824T174736Z-d428af9e8413115e","text":"named_ids catches _TREE_PARSE_ERRORS like the other tree readers, including AttributeError when a children-file child is not a mapping.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"58d640914b470b3e","sum":"Root wake prints how_to under Usage and catalogs other stores; skip a second root wake when that Usage block is still readable. Onboarding is init (bootstrap only); 3.11 floor is right after import sys.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"5672e8d92ee69a50","sum":"equal_grain_pair is fold-test only; 3.11 floor is right after import sys (#42). Root wake prints how_to_text under Usage; AGENTS.md is bootstrap only.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"61fbb8f64668e9b1","sum":"equal_grain_pair is a fold-test oracle only; fold_request walks adjacent same-grain ViewNodes itself; sys.version_info is immediately after import sys so 3.10 prints the floor message instead of ModuleNotFoundError.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260824T174900Z-adbb0c6c6a991bca","text":"equal_grain_pair is a fold-test oracle only; the copied driver does not keep it. fold_request still walks adjacent same-grain ViewNodes itself.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260824T174934Z-b3f3d92f255bc910","text":"summem checks sys.version_info immediately after import sys and before import tomllib; Python 3.10 prints SumMem needs Python 3.11 or newer instead of ModuleNotFoundError.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"9f3b2086879920a2","sum":"3.11 floor is import-time before tomllib (#42/#38). Root wake prints how_to_text under Usage; AGENTS.md is bootstrap only (wake-if-needed, note, writer-only).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260824T175246Z-a3c8d06b34d1a7c4","text":"PR #42 feat/require-python closes #38: import-time 3.11 floor before tomllib; Python 3.10 prints SumMem needs Python 3.11 or newer.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260825T003315Z-1061fd623922ceb6","text":"Root wake prints how_to_text under == SumMem Usage ==; the AGENTS.md prefix is the bootstrap only (wake-if-needed, note, writer-only).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"dcff76f4cde304af","sum":"Skip a root wake only when a == SumMem Usage == block is still readable. Onboarding is init: prints the bootstrap (prompt_text()), writes nothing; replace an old fat AGENTS.md prefix once. A consumer upgrade is copying the script. Root-wake catalog tests slice that section.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"961801789374c217","sum":"Skip a root wake only when a == SumMem Usage == block is still readable. A consumer upgrade is copying the script; init prints the bootstrap and writes nothing; replace an old fat AGENTS.md prefix once.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260825T003337Z-7415cd62d790d57b","text":"Skip a root wake when a == SumMem Usage == block is still readable; do not skip on a remembered wake or the footer alone.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260825T003343Z-32520d7e11eb7ac8","text":"A consumer upgrade is copying the script; replace an old fat AGENTS.md prefix once. init prints the bootstrap and writes nothing.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"d0629b8c4f7d147a","sum":"Onboarding is init (prompt_text()); root-wake catalog tests slice the catalog section.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260825T004057Z-33f2fad52281ba51","text":"Root-wake tests that pin catalog shape must slice the catalog section; Usage contains .summem/summem and wake --path.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260825T133725Z-1b75d9fa0073870a","text":"Onboarding is summem init (prompt_text()); there is no docs/agents-prompt.md copy.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"a01e0246698076f2","sum":"Nap captions are .summ. SLOBAC: proofs stay; 3.11 floor (no CI 3.10); findings 14, 60-63 kept (PR #48). Zoom pin is the selected nap's two public wake lines. Catalog is git-visible /.summem/ paths; recall/zoom unique-prefix once, parse each view .tree once; heal is raw JSON.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"023ef6d783b9ba73","sum":"Nap captions are .summ, not .sum. SLOBAC 2026-08-25 ratchet (proofs stay; 3.11 floor because CI has no 3.10). Process-level tests renamed off test_proof_*; zoom pin is the selected nap's two public wake lines. slobac-audit-ratchet archived PR #48 (findings 14, 60-63 kept).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"445d51b96a604dfb","sum":"Nap captions are .summ, not .sum; leftover .sum is not a caption. SLOBAC 2026-08-25 ratchet applied (proofs stay; 3.11 floor because CI has no 3.10). Consumer .sum→.summ find recipe was on PR #47.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"fadfed630d13aa36","sum":"Nap captions are .summ, not .sum; leftover .sum beside a .tree is not a caption. Consumer find recipe is on PR #47 for the squash BREAKING CHANGES footer.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260825T153120Z-33fb53e74d638a8e","text":"Nap caption files are .summ; a leftover .sum beside a .tree is not a caption.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260825T160856Z-79b76d35d66fe702","text":"summ-caption-suffix archived: captions are .summ; consumer find recipe on PR #47 for squash BREAKING CHANGES.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"7d9b22491a29a836","sum":"SLOBAC 2026-08-25 audit (284 tests) found 63 smells; ratchet applied. Proofs stay as file-backend acceptance; the 3.11-floor pin stays because CI has no 3.10.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260825T174056Z-e79674666263e761","text":"2026-08-25 SLOBAC all-smells audit of tests/ (284 tests): 63 deduplicated findings; largest clusters loose-text-oracle 30, vacuous-assertion 12, implementation-coupled 10; cross-suite confirmed 4 redundancies and proof-file fossils.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260825T180628Z-7d45f92e68433516","text":"SLOBAC 2026-08-25 ratchet applied to tests: proofs kept as file-backend acceptance; CI has no 3.10 so the source-order 3.11-floor pin stays.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"81969101cc5f4d48","sum":"Process-level tests renamed off test_proof_*; zoom pin is the selected nap's two public wake lines. slobac-audit-ratchet archived (19 fixes, PR #48; findings 14, 60-63 kept). Perf @5k: wake ~1ms, startup ~120ms, heal 81ms, recall short_id 19s, catalog walk 44ms vs ls-files 2.5ms","tree":{"c":[{"id":"a4ec8912daa1494d","sum":"Process-level tests renamed off test_proof_*; zoom pin is the selected nap's two public wake lines; tox py311-py314 was 284.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260825T181644Z-3f292cfab0ac6216","text":"Process-level tests renamed off test_proof_*: worktree merge, caption conflict, squash-clone zoom, nap reject, branch-pack merge, path walk-up and catalog. First proof N gone.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260825T185219Z-e6bb937a75148bd1","text":"QA PASS: test_zoom_expanded_child_id pins the selected nap's exact two public wake lines; tox py311-py314 each pass 284 tests.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"aa3c608f961e94cc","sum":"slobac-audit-ratchet archived: 19 fixes + PR #48 zoom pin; findings 14 and 60-63 kept. Perf audit @5k: wake ~1ms; startup ~120ms; heal 81ms/note; recall short_id 19s; catalog walk 44ms vs git ls-files 2.5ms","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260825T185552Z-c63aabf42fe2467f","text":"slobac-audit-ratchet archived: 19 ratchet fixes + Phase A rename + PR #48 zoom pin; findings 14 and 60-63 kept; memory-bank/archive/enhancements/20260825-slobac-audit-ratchet.md","type":"note"},{"name":"20260825T191431Z-3c64d129c6c9a0bb","text":"Perf audit: wake view ~1ms@5k leaves. Costs: ~120ms startup (compile 29ms; dataclasses/argparse/tomllib imports), heal reparses every .tree per note (81ms@5k), recall per-line short_id rescan (19s@5k common word), catalog os.walk+check-ignore 44ms vs git ls-files 2.5ms","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"107070bb94d80d9b","sum":"Perf shards: catalog is one git ls-files of .summem/config.toml; recall/zoom unique-prefix once (sort+neighbor LCP) and parse each view .tree once; named_ids shares that walk. Heal overlap is raw JSON; rematerialize/write_nap build Tree. Wave #49∥#50 then #51 then #53 then #52.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"78d34186f9c1d621","sum":"Perf shards #49/#50: catalog via one git ls-files of .summem/config.toml; recall/zoom unique-prefix once (sort+neighbor LCP) and parse each view .tree at most once; named_ids shares that walk. Wave was #49∥#50 then #51 then #53 then #52.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"0302e7603c8f235a","sum":"Perf shards filed: #49 catalog ls-files, #50 recall/zoom prefix+parse-once, #51 heal raw-JSON, #52 drop-dataclasses, #53 skip-heal (design). Wave #49∥#50 then #51 then #53 then #52; close/defer ok.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260825T192652Z-f5aecd1900237e75","text":"Perf shards filed: #49 catalog ls-files, #50 recall/zoom prefix+parse-once, #51 heal raw-JSON walk, #52 startup dataclasses/lazy-import, #53 skip-heal marker (design)","type":"note"},{"name":"20260825T193539Z-a762122c1565c2e3","text":"perf-shards L4: #49∥#50 then #51 then #53 then #52; parent operator; close/defer ok; parent L4 files stay off main until capstone.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f05f9b5376fd649a","sum":"Issues #49/#50: catalog via one git ls-files of .summem/config.toml; recall/zoom unique-prefix once (sort+neighbor LCP) and parse each view .tree at most once; named_ids shares that walk.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260825T193914Z-a87c411d06c19c31","text":"Issue #50: recall/zoom unique-prefix once per command (sort+neighbor LCP) and parse each view .tree at most once; named_ids shares that walk. Catalog/heal/dataclasses stay out.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260825T193954Z-611094457cb3dfa9","text":"Issue #49 plan: catalog_text becomes one git ls-files -z --cached --others --exclude-standard filtered for .summem/config.toml; _ignored_store goes away.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"3def4ffb3ddeacd7","sum":"Catalog is one git ls-files of .summem/config.toml; recall/zoom unique-prefix once and parse each view .tree once (#50). Heal overlap is raw JSON; rematerialize and write_nap still build Tree (#51/#56).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"fb6c804b59655564","sum":"catalog is one git ls-files of .summem/config.toml; recall/zoom unique-prefix once and parse each view .tree once (#50).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260825T195218Z-f3eba96c79b9d954","text":"Root catalog enumerates via one git ls-files --cached --others --exclude-standard filtered on .summem/config.toml; no committed index.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260825T200439Z-dff2e8353bdc9000","text":"recall-zoom-prefix archived: recall/zoom unique-prefix once per command (sort+neighbor LCP) and parse each view .tree at most once; named_ids shares that walk. Issue #50.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f3a4c22a002e4dd6","sum":"heal overlap is raw JSON; rematerialize and write_nap still build Tree. PR #56 Fixes #51.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260825T200855Z-2670ea812d7405e3","text":"Issue #51: heal digest walk is raw JSON only; rematerialize and write_nap still build Tree when writing a pack.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260825T202339Z-0c3a676acf423f91","text":"Heal overlap checks walk raw tree JSON; note/nap thread one list_view and knobs. PR #56 Fixes #51.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"d4a72c32501c87cd","sum":"slots+lazy imports; wake never cuts; 5-part 16-hex stems, lex-greatest (migrate.py reads old); tox run-parallel py311-314, coverage serial; fold_request text only, ids on Run:; Usage owns argv; leaf_digests no-overlap, same-text->later; CRLF->LF; flock naps/; N: counts leaves","tree":{"c":[{"id":"9c3bc303738a33f4","sum":"slots+lazy imports; wake never cuts; five-part nap stems, zipper lex-greatest; migrate.py sole old-stem reader (4/5-part-64); tox run-parallel, pytest -n auto --maxprocesses=4, coverage serial; CI py311–314; 16-hex leafset; nap-ack Saved. then fold or idle","tree":{"c":[{"id":"e0605938272b7cd2","sum":"slots not dataclasses; lazy optional imports; wake never cuts over-budget views; five-part nap stems (seq-leafset-grain-variant), four-part is a prefix so lex heal needs no branch; zipper keeps lex-greatest; migrate.py is the sole old-stem reader","tree":{"c":[{"id":"7c5ef48db5fe3c10","sum":"drop-dataclasses: slots + lazy imports; version/init/-h omit optional imports; 3.14 import tracing; perf-shards #49-52 shipped (#53 deferred); same-leaf-set conflicts keep one variant; wake never cuts over-budget views.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"ad4caf8a4e44a08e","sum":"PR #55: zoom pack map by node.name; catalog treats git-visible /.summem/ paths as started stores. drop-dataclasses: slots + lazy tomllib/fcntl/subprocess/random/argparse; version/init/-h skip those; 3.14 traces driver __import__","tree":{"c":[{"id":"ee4b855f3bb41c18","sum":"PR #55 zoom pack map by node.name; catalog treats git-visible /.summem/ paths as started stores, not only config.toml","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260825T202720Z-e2156bfaebf2808e","text":"PR #55 review: zoom pack map keyed by node.name so a shared content id prints the first list_view row; _index_tree inside loads_tree try so unprojectable children skip like other unreadable packs.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260825T202837Z-054930bcd901bdc3","text":"Root catalog treats any git-visible path under /.summem/ as a started store, not only config.toml; file-level ignore of config.toml cannot hide a store that has notes.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ba93ada09ab368a1","sum":"drop-dataclasses: slots + lazy tomllib/fcntl/subprocess/random/argparse; version/init/-h skip those imports; 3.14 isolation traces driver __import__, not fcntl absent from sys.modules","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260825T203211Z-4806c48701ff1fd1","text":"Issue #52 L2 drop-dataclasses: slots for five types + lazy tomllib/fcntl/subprocess/random; version/init/help must not import those three; 3.11 gate stays after import sys; argparse leftover optional","type":"note"},{"name":"20260825T204312Z-499edef570adadd5","text":"3.14 pathlib imports fcntl; startup isolation tests must trace the driver's __import__, not assert fcntl absent from sys.modules","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"cf60f219a2792389","sum":"drop-dataclasses: slots + lazy imports, 3.14 traces driver imports; perf-shards #49-52 shipped, #53 deferred; same-leaf-set conflicts take one side's .summem paths; wake never drops nodes to fit WAKE_LINES.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"487ebdfd573e5b55","sum":"drop-dataclasses archived: slots + lazy imports; py3.14 startup traces driver imports. perf-shards L4 archived: #49-52 merged via #54-57; #53 deferred (heal ~1ms, stem-hash cannot skip note).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260825T204853Z-9fffd75ba86574c8","text":"drop-dataclasses archived: slots + lazy tomllib/fcntl/subprocess/random/argparse; version/init/-h skip those imports; 3.14 isolation traces driver __import__; memory-bank/archive/enhancements/20260825-drop-dataclasses.md","type":"note"},{"name":"20260825T213440Z-4f6d26cb15712799","text":"perf-shards L4 archived to memory-bank/archive/systems/20260825-perf-shards.md; #49–#52 merged as #54–#57; #53 won't-do-YET (leftover heal ~1ms; stem-hash cannot skip note).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"b8d0c71e201b6a9e","sum":"Conflicting same-leaf-set naps: take every .summem path from one side; wake never drops view nodes to fit WAKE_LINES — over-budget lists all until note/nap fold.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260825T213542Z-65041798fe3dbbfa","text":"Same leaf-set id with different nested captions add/add-conflicts both .tree and .summ; never mismatch a stem; take every conflicting .summem path from one side (#59).","type":"note"},{"name":"20260825T221202Z-91f4493afe6aed99","text":"Wake never drops view nodes to fit WAKE_LINES; over-budget (including 0) lists every node; note/nap fold the count back.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ad7350b1d6b9b2cd","sum":"Nap stems are five-part seq-leafset-grain-pair-digest; a four-part stem is a prefix of its five-part twin so lex heal needs no format branch; zipper keeps lex-greatest; driver reads five-part only, migrate.py is the sole four-part reader; child_nap_stem names rematerialize.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"90d7e5acee519c7f","sum":"Nap stems are five-part seq-leafset-grain-pair-digest; zipper keeps lex-greatest; migrate.py (operator-only, sibling-load by __file__) rewrites old stems. #61 supersedes #59; wake-never-cut archived as #60.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"820f42beb587e299","sum":"wake-never-cut archived (#60); Issue #61 added five-part nap stems with pair-byte variants; migrate.py is an operator-only surgery analogue.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260825T222443Z-9e0ebfff2047eda7","text":"wake-never-cut archived to memory-bank/archive/bug-fixes/20260825-wake-never-cut.md; draft PR #60.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260825T230722Z-c53313e27e6b7b27","text":"Issue #61 L3: five-part nap stems with pair-bytes variant tag; operator migrate.py is a surgery analogue, not a summem verb.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"2ce00208bcbe0278","sum":"Nap stems are five-part seq-leafset-grain-pair-digest; zipper keeps lex-greatest; migrate rewrites old stems. nap-variant-stems QA: 346 tests. surgery.plan_break_out duplicates child-stem logic; migrate loads sibling summem by __file__ from cwd.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260826T001753Z-7316415cc5604024","text":"Nap stems are five-part {seq}-{leafset}-{grain}-{pair-digest}; git unions same-block variants; zipper keeps the lex-greatest; migrate.py rewrites four-part stores.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260826T002702Z-26707560339bbbf7","text":"QA PASS nap-variant-stems (346 tests py311-314). surgery.plan_break_out duplicates rematerialize_child's child-stem block with no test pinning them equal. migrate.py loads sibling summem by __file__ and takes its store from cwd.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"cf83f26b93a1e0ab","sum":"Four-part nap stem is a prefix of its five-part twin so lex heal needs no format branch; driver lists five-part stems only and migrate.py is the only four-part reader; child_nap_stem names rematerialize and surgery; started_stores lists git root only when .summem is a directory.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"0f04308dc7e8c4c7","sum":"Nap-variant-stems: four-part stem is a prefix of its five-part twin so lex heal needs no format branch; child_nap_stem names rematerialize and surgery; started_stores lists git root only when .summem is a directory.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260826T003014Z-adbfa7448201be34","text":"Nap-variant-stems reflected: QA PASS, 346 tests; a four-part stem is a prefix of its five-part twin so lex heal needs no format branch.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260826T004034Z-6b4ff0568eccf9a6","text":"child_nap_stem is the shared serialize-then-name path for rematerialize and surgery; started_stores lists the git root only when .summem is a directory.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"8ebfa75808b2336c","sum":"Driver lists five-part nap stems only; migrate.py is the only four-part reader.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260826T004244Z-cbe9baa615b860a5","text":"PR #62 is the five-part nap-stem draft; closes #61 and supersedes #59.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260826T005232Z-a1d8ce977ef75db8","text":"Clean break: driver lists five-part nap stems only; migrate.py is the only four-part reader.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"471f0eb93e28d342","sum":"Local tox run-parallel, session fixture, no --basetemp; env pytest -n auto --maxprocesses=4; coverage serial; PR CI pr.yaml 311–314, main ci.yaml+coverage; 16-hex leafset, migrate.py only 4/5-part-64 reader; nap-ack Saved. then fold or idle","tree":{"c":[{"id":"4545e77a54ec6e77","sum":"Local tox: run-parallel, session fixture, no --basetemp; env pytest -n auto --maxprocesses=4; coverage serial. PR CI is pr.yaml py311–py314; main is ci.yaml plus coverage. #65/#66 closed #63/#64.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"45cf7d8ae1c3a941","sum":"local tox: run-parallel, session fixture, no --basetemp; CI matrix on PR, coverage only on main","tree":{"c":[{"id":"36328cf904c2428a","sum":"local tox: run-parallel, session fixture, no --basetemp; nap-variant-stems archived","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260826T010300Z-417024a4752a8337","text":"nap-variant-stems archived to memory-bank/archive/enhancements/20260825-nap-variant-stems.md; draft PR #62; PR review all dismissed","type":"note"},{"name":"20260826T012700Z-be1b409a2bdf91a3","text":"Full local tox is tox run-parallel; pytest --basetemp is TMPDIR/summem-{env} so outside-repo tests stay outside the clone; tests load summem via a session fixture.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e9d850f97d191356","sum":"tox: run-parallel locally, no --basetemp, session fixture; CI matrix on PR, coverage only on main","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260826T014547Z-7e85524296498ed1","text":"Full local tox is tox run-parallel; do not pass pytest --basetemp (default already isolates outside the clone). Tests cache summem in conftest._SUMMEM because migrate.py and surgery.py overwrite sys.modules['summem'].","type":"note"},{"name":"20260826T020511Z-dedaa99398372c27","text":"CI runs tox py311-py314 on pull requests and on main; tox -e coverage and the Codecov upload run only on pushes to main.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ac119d66989496d0","sum":"Local tox: run-parallel; each env pytest -n auto --maxprocesses=4; coverage serial. PR CI is pr.yaml (py311–py314); main is ci.yaml plus coverage. #65 closed #63; #66 closed #64.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"d3a518852906da6f","sum":"Local tox: run-parallel, session fixture. PR CI is .github/workflows/pr.yaml (py311–py314); main is ci.yaml plus coverage. tox-speedup archived; PR #65 closed #63.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260826T020911Z-dc61c4600974926c","text":"PR checks are .github/workflows/pr.yaml (tox py311-py314). Main CI is .github/workflows/ci.yaml (same matrix plus coverage upload).","type":"note"},{"name":"20260826T021234Z-bd17f467296b95fc","text":"tox-speedup archived: local tox run-parallel, session summem fixture, PR/ci workflow split. Draft PR #65 closes #63.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"4ef12b6001b08fed","sum":"Each tox env is pytest -n auto --maxprocesses=4; coverage stays serial; 0 serial markers; PR #66 closes #64.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260826T024233Z-b9bc41aef5017da0","text":"Each tox env runs pytest -n auto --maxprocesses=4; coverage stays serial. Serial markers: 0. Unbounded auto made tox run-parallel slower.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260826T030409Z-e8788d730d1e85ab","text":"pytest-xdist archived: each tox env is -n auto --maxprocesses=4; 0 serial markers; PR #66 closes #64.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"143544e6ec1e6aa3","sum":"16-hex leafset (SHA-256[:16]); migrate.py only 4/5-part-64 reader; first birthday is a widen PR; atlas Identity is the line; nap-ack: Saved. then fold or idle","tree":{"c":[{"id":"f8e4c51c47553dd2","sum":"16-hex (#67): SHA-256[:16] in leafset_id, stems, nested NapChild.id; migrate.py is the only 4-part and 5-part-64 reader; first birthday is a widen PR. README walkthrough still shows a 64-hex pair name; atlas Identity is the real line.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"a6d10958ef7a6ee6","sum":"16-hex leafset (#67): store ids are SHA-256[:16]; migrate.py rewrites 4-part and 5-part-64 (nested ids, new variant); first birthday is a widen PR, do not pre-empt.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260826T030848Z-6dd27b032a8f016d","text":"Issue #67: stored leaf-set ids become 16 hex; migrate.py consumes 4-part and 5-part-64 stems, writes 5-part-16 only (rewrite nested .tree ids, recompute variant).","type":"note"},{"name":"20260826T031521Z-7a97f5ab2c7bcdc0","text":"16-hex leafset (#67): whoever first hits the birthday sends a PR that widens the field and adds a new migrate.py; do not pre-empt.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"4f3e636fac243401","sum":"16-hex (#67): one width in leafset_id for view ids, stems, nested NapChild.id; migrate.py is the only 4-part and 5-part-64 reader. README walkthrough still shows a 64-hex pair name; atlas Identity is the real line.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260826T032419Z-eb9e2bbccde1ebf1","text":"16-hex leafset (#67): truncate inside leafset_id so note view ids, nap stems, and nested NapChild.id share one width; migrate.py is the only 4-part and 5-part-64 reader.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260826T033238Z-2920440793dd567a","text":"Preflight #67: README on-disk walkthrough still shows a 64-hex leaf-set in the pair basename; there is no in-tree #61 do-not-shorten sentence — atlas Identity 'Stored names keep the full id' is the real line.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"851029656cfd973f","sum":"16-hex-leafset archived; nap-ack prints Saved. then fold or idle","tree":{"c":[{"id":"60d6151770f06a24","sum":"16-hex-leafset built then archived; PR #68 review-clean, ready to merge and close #67","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260826T042031Z-6b03a81f7ebe2424","text":"16-hex-leafset built: leafset_id is SHA-256[:16]; migrate.py rewrites 4-part-64 and 5-part-64 (nested ids, new variant); root and dogfood stores migrated.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260826T131401Z-803adc196488671b","text":"16-hex-leafset archived; PR #68 review-clean (incl. CodeRabbit), ready to merge and close #67","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"96eb80a6d5d89d9a","sum":"nap-ack: Saved. then fold or idle; ratchet stays silent","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260828T153444Z-2d2f206f379e45f2","text":"nap-ack L2: successful nap prints Saved. then fold or Nothing left to compress; ENTRY_CHARS ratchet still silent","type":"note"},{"name":"20260828T155248Z-8215d9d28b8c6de4","text":"nap-ack: successful nap prints Saved. then fold or Nothing left to compress; ratchet stays silent; idle is nap-only","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1d306fce42373cd7","sum":"fold_request: text only, ids on Run:. Repo-only membership (skip PR/checks/archive). Editable init/AGENTS.md lockstep; Usage owns argv; wording unpinned. leafset_id/leaf_digests; no overlap, same-text->later #77. CRLF->LF; flock naps/ else runtime-dir; N: ./path counts leaves.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"09440533b9d582ef","sum":"fold_request quotes captions only; ids on Run: and wake. Membership is this repo, not this clone; skip PR opened, checks passed, task archived. Write rule is editable init/AGENTS.md; Usage owns argv. Wording unpinned except AGENTS.md lockstep. Leaves: leafset_id, leaf_digests.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"7bdadb9eac2d17e2","sum":"fold_request quotes captions without grain or prefix; ids stay on Run: and wake. Membership: this repository, not this clone; denylist: PR opened / checks passed / task archived. Keep prompt_text and how_to_text direct; AGENTS.md lockstep; do not factor MEMBERSHIP_PROBE.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"f3167b0d6e37b6f8","sum":"fold_request quotes captions without grain or prefix; ids stay on Run: and wake. nap-ack archived PR #70 in 0.10.0; fold-pack-captions archived PR #72.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"5324ef472b747f57","sum":"nap-ack archived PR #70 in 0.10.0; fold_request quotes captions without grain or prefix; ids stay on Run: and wake","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260828T203321Z-c2a6d088a4562375","text":"nap-ack archived to memory-bank/archive/enhancements/20260828-nap-ack.md; PR #70 shipped in 0.10.0","type":"note"},{"name":"20260828T204506Z-31f09329ef4334ce","text":"fold_request quotes pack captions without grain or prefix; ids stay on Run: and on wake","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"615d4dde9f0c32a6","sum":"fold-pack-captions: QA PASS (captions-only pack quotes; Run ids, wake grammar, dated leaf quotes, blank missing captions); archived to memory-bank/archive/enhancements/20260828-fold-pack-captions.md; PR #72 shipped","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260828T204631Z-e522d85fd7832cb5","text":"QA PASS fold-pack-captions: captions-only pack quotes; Run ids, wake grammar, dated leaf quotes, and blank missing captions verified.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260828T221517Z-3d32badb9e14e803","text":"fold-pack-captions archived to memory-bank/archive/enhancements/20260828-fold-pack-captions.md; PR #72 shipped","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"875be840dc360726","sum":"Membership: work on this repository, not this clone; how-to denylist is PR opened / checks passed / task archived. Keep the short phrase direct in prompt_text and how_to_text; AGENTS.md lockstep; factoring MEMBERSHIP_PROBE is not worth it.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"6d3d53d6fdf41b4e","sum":"Membership: another contributor needs it to work on this repository, not in this clone; how-to denylist is PR opened / checks passed / task archived.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260828T224532Z-bccf1887bea608d5","text":"note membership probe is work in this clone; how-to denylist is PR opened / checks passed / task archived","type":"note"},{"name":"20260829T000716Z-4f13dab49598cbb6","text":"Membership wording: say 'work on this repository', not 'work in this clone'; contributors have separate checkouts.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"24fb43f4be5c6f63","sum":"prompt_text and how_to_text keep the short membership phrase direct; AGENTS.md lockstep covers the bootstrap copy. Factoring MEMBERSHIP_PROBE harms readability for negligible benefit.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260829T001244Z-53dde24650751d3f","text":"prompt_text and how_to_text share MEMBERSHIP_PROBE; AGENTS.md lockstep covers the bootstrap copy.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260829T002301Z-2fe1954978d4b4e4","text":"Keep the short membership phrase direct in prompt_text and how_to_text; factoring it harms readability for negligible benefit.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"99582cfe7bce97c1","sum":"Write rule lives only in editable init/AGENTS.md; wake Usage is mechanics, owns its argv, and fold_request prints the exact Run: line. Prompt wording is unpinned except AGENTS.md lockstep. Leaf identity is leafset_id and leaf_digests; heal may drop a packed loose note (#77).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"6cee800557d99eac","sum":"Write rule lives only in init/AGENTS.md as editable policy; wake Usage is mechanics only. Usage owns every argv it claims; fold_request prints the exact Run: line. Prompt and write-rule wording are not pinned, only AGENTS.md lockstep and init identity; prefix teaches no argv.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"44e244aef3c74c04","sum":"Write rule lives only in init/AGENTS.md as editable policy; wake Usage is mechanics only (repeating membership would override a consumer's gate). Usage owns every argv it claims; fold_request prints the exact Run: line; Usage must not say Run:.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260829T164055Z-10a43354ce0f7523","text":"Creative: write rule lives only in init/AGENTS.md as editable policy; wake Usage is mechanics only; repeating membership on wake would override a consumer's gate.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260829T170414Z-a3069e4d545d0246","text":"Usage owns every argv it claims: note, nap ID-A ID-B CAPTION, recall, zoom, wake --path. fold_request still prints the exact Run: line; Usage must not say Run:","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"750292c631261ac3","sum":"prompt_text and write-rule wording are not pinned; only AGENTS.md prefix lockstep and init identity are. Prefix must not teach note/nap argv or Usage recipes; fold_request prints the exact Run: line; invoked as {AGENT_BIN} is not a recipe.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260829T204616Z-0c23f7c61b19009e","text":"prompt_text wording is not pinned; only AGENTS.md prefix lockstep and init identity. Prefix must not teach note/nap argv or Usage recipes.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260829T210418Z-1a2dc36f0829c667","text":"Usage does not teach nap argv; fold_request still prints the exact Run: line. Prefix may say invoked as {AGENT_BIN}; that is not a recipe. Write-rule wording is not pinned — AGENTS.md lockstep and init identity are.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"4d7aff95d7826e88","sum":"Leaf identity is content: leafset_id keys the multiset, leaf_digests the set. Heal dropping a packed-text loose note is the #77 shoebox, intended. Theory names the system; the leak may name those two functions.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"921a29be1c45a6be","sum":"Leaf identity is content: leafset_id keys the multiset, leaf_digests the set. Heal dropping a packed-text loose note is the #77 shoebox. Theory names the system; the leak may name those two functions. Do not cite notes.md for that judgement.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260829T211122Z-ad3d3bf48d2c3470","text":"Leaf identity is content-only: heal drops a loose note whose text already sits inside a pack, silently deleting a just-written note (#77). leafset_id keys on the multiset; leaf_digests keys on the set.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260829T214451Z-1d8350664f6c3f7d","text":"theory.md argues why it converges: name the system, not summem:line. Architecture owns filenames and functions. Exception: the #77 leak names leafset_id vs leaf_digests because that disagreement is the defect. Do not cite notes.md from 'leaving the cut open is a judgement'.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"20725fd9d9689622","sum":"Leaf identity is content (L is a set of facts), not per-file name+bytes; heal dropping a packed-text loose note is the #77 shoebox, intended, not a bug.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260829T220028Z-01040c6fdd23aa89","text":"Leaf identity is per-file (name + bytes); two recordings of one sentence are two leaves (#77)","type":"note"},{"name":"20260829T220314Z-0fd6a303482b711a","text":"L is a set of facts (content); heal dropping a packed-text loose note is the shoebox, not a bug. #77 trigger 1 is intended.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"a3a1b9be97f9acf5","sum":"No intersecting digests; same-text heals to later file #77. fold_request: text only; ids on Run:. CRLF as LF. flock naps/, else runtime-dir; msvcrt 30s. No os.name=nt. python .summem/summem wake. Win AGENTS.md: Unix, unadvertised. N: ./path note+1, nap leaves once. Saved. is ACK.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"8879531bae2973c5","sum":"write_nap rejects intersecting digest sets; same-text loose notes heal to the later file (#77). fold_request quotes text only; grain/date on wake/recall/zoom; ids on Run:. -h documents --path. Windows: stock AGENTS.md stays Unix, unadvertised; Run: prints host invoke; CRLF->LF","tree":{"c":[{"id":"c0b91843eda5c237","sum":"write_nap rejects intersecting digest sets; identical loose notes heal to the later filename (#77). fold_request quotes caption/note text only; grain and date stay on wake, recall, zoom; ids stay on Run:. No nested stores: root wake omits catalog how-to; -h documents --path.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"edb0ea0fb012e074","sum":"write_nap rejects intersecting digest sets; identical loose notes heal to the later filename (#77)","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260829T223329Z-dff4d96e7ee27dcc","text":"write_nap rejects any intersecting digest sets; two identical loose notes collapse on heal to the later filename (#77)","type":"note"},{"name":"20260829T230843Z-3ad41bcf17625899","text":"heal-same-text archived to memory-bank/archive/bug-fixes/20260829-heal-same-text.md; PR #79","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ec999124e9bbfbf6","sum":"fold_request quotes caption/note text only; grain and date stay on wake, recall, and zoom; ids stay on Run:. With no nested stores, root wake omits catalog how-to; -h still documents --path.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260829T232955Z-ce112a8dc2e0252b","text":"fold_request quotes caption/note text only; grain and date stay on wake, recall, zoom; ids stay on Run:","type":"note"},{"name":"20260903T213935Z-aa0196fbeb246257","text":"Root wake omits catalog how-to when no nested stores exist; operator -h still documents --path.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"34adeab4ac984330","sum":"Windows: AGENTS.md clone-portable, stock stays Unix; do not advertise native support (no argv0 runs in both cmd.exe and Unix). Usage/Run: print host invoke (sys.executable). Lock and CRLF-on-read let a shop patch its bootstrap; no consumer .gitattributes, no store lock file.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"819660f9289867d7","sum":"Windows: AGENTS.md clone-portable (no C:\\ argv0; not pasteable). Usage/Run may print host invoke. note/nap crash on import fcntl; pathlib --path and python .summem/summem work; no store lock file. No consumer .gitattributes; canonicalize CRLF on read; punt this-repo git symlink.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260910T005128Z-e234bb60ff9049ba","text":"Windows: AGENTS.md stays clone-portable (no C:\\ argv0); Usage/Run: may print host invoke. note/nap crash on import fcntl; pathlib --path and python .summem/summem work; do not flock a store lock file.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260910T010940Z-0a0daf8323fd00b0","text":"Windows port: no consumer .gitattributes — canonicalize CRLF on read for digest/JSON; punt this-repo git symlink; AGENTS.md is not a pasteable argv0.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"597efaa40d5ae61b","sum":"Windows: do not advertise native support (no argv0 runs in both cmd.exe and Unix shells); internals (lock, CRLF) let a Windows shop patch its bootstrap. Usage/Run: print the host invoke (sys.executable); stock AGENTS.md stays Unix.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260910T011527Z-a89670306f0346b1","text":"Do not advertise native Windows: no argv0 is a command in both cmd.exe and a Unix shell. Ceiling is internals (lock, CRLF) so a Windows-only shop can patch their bootstrap.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260910T011559Z-5a487f135c8e6892","text":"Windows: print host-specific invoke on Usage/Run: (sys.executable). Stock AGENTS.md stays Unix; only a shop that patched the bootstrap will see the Windows lines.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c1b15455613b38c1","sum":"CRLF as LF on read. Lock: flock naps/, else runtime-dir; msvcrt 30s, slack 1e-9. Never monkeypatch os.name to nt. python .summem/summem wake; names no path. Usage bare Unix, python Windows. N: ./path (note +1, nap leaves once). --path walks up. Nap line sequences; Saved. is ACK.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"5c6784a8f49cfad6","sum":"Windows: CRLF canonicalized on read; lock is naps/ flock else runtime-dir file, msvcrt wait 30s monotonic (test allows 1e-9 slack). Bootstrap wake is python .summem/summem wake; Usage bare on Unix, python-prefixed on Windows. Never monkeypatch os.name to nt on Linux.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"278f6b06c3a7df2f","sum":"Windows: CRLF canonicalized on read; lock is naps/ flock, else a runtime-dir file (fcntl then msvcrt); msvcrt wait is 30s monotonic elapsed, waited += 0.01 is backoff only. Do not monkeypatch os.name to nt on Linux (WindowsPath crash).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260910T014746Z-2240e9a38cbd40b5","text":"Windows: CRLF canonicalize on read; lock is naps/ flock else runtime-dir file (fcntl then msvcrt); do not monkeypatch os.name to nt on Linux (pathlib WindowsPath crash).","type":"note"},{"name":"20260910T153140Z-a4f303a1f756c0ca","text":"msvcrt lock wait is 30s monotonic elapsed; waited += 0.01 is backoff only, not the deadline","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"2bc6b5f9386d965f","sum":"Bootstrap wake is python .summem/summem wake; Usage is bare on Unix, python-prefixed on Windows. msvcrt lock-deadline test allows 1e-9 slack on sum(sleeps): 3.12+ can land at 30.000000000000007.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260910T234518Z-6ee83d5cd5f8d318","text":"Bootstrap wake is python .summem/summem wake; Usage is bare on Unix, python-prefixed on Windows","type":"note"},{"name":"20260910T234852Z-a4967a2ed0a2a1f1","text":"msvcrt lock-deadline test must allow 1e-9 slack on sum(sleeps); 3.12+ can land at 30.000000000000007","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"2dfeefe80535b269","sum":"First wake is python .summem/summem wake; the intro names no invoked-as path. Catalog lines are N: ./path, N a count from one ls-files pass (loose note +1, nap stem its leaves once). --path walks up to the nearest store. Usage nap line is sequencing only; Saved. owns the ACK.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"8a207191a07b0eec","sum":"First wake is python .summem/summem wake; the prompt intro names no invoked-as path. Root catalog lines are N: ./path, N the filename leaf grain from one ls-files pass (loose note +1, nap stem once).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260911T001036Z-0b56b4cb6829c2f7","text":"prompt_text intro is managed through SumMem only; first-wake is python .summem/summem wake; no invoked-as path","type":"note"},{"name":"20260915T225419Z-4b8f0ca4ed1bdaaf","text":"Root catalog lines are N: ./path; N is filename leaf grain from the same ls-files pass (loose note +1, nap stem once). Path is the ./ token.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"784324e867a813e8","sum":"Catalog N: is a count; --path on note, nap, recall, zoom walks up to the nearest store. Usage nap line is sequencing only; Saved. owns the ACK (no already-stored or do-not-retry).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260915T230226Z-c1e5723514aa52a8","text":"Catalog how-to: N: is a count; note --path <file> walks up to the nearest store. Same --path on nap, recall, zoom.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260915T230920Z-fd73dce7353c1e73","text":"Usage nap line is sequencing only; Saved. owns ACK (no already-stored / do-not-retry).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
